    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_purpose">Śodhamitra — Research Planner is a private workspace that helps scholars plan, organise and document their research. It works entirely on this device.</string>
    <string name="about_sections">It has three main sections: PhD Research, Individual Researcher / Author, and Editing / Translation Planner.</string>
    <string name="about_projects">In PhD Research and Individual Researcher / Author you create projects and build a Thesis Outline or Book Outline: chapters, points under each chapter, and a description of any length for every point.</string>
    <string name="about_notes">Individual Researcher / Author projects also hold Research Notes, together with References / Citations to books, manuscripts and articles, including page or folio numbers and contextual notes.</string>
    <string name="about_bibliography">PhD Research projects keep a Bibliography of books, manuscripts and articles. Manuscripts are described with one shared form wherever they appear.</string>
    <string name="about_planner">Editing / Translation Planner keeps a Future Editing List (manuscripts and books) and a Future Trans List (books) as tables.</string>
    <string name="about_languages">The interface is available in ten languages: English, Kannada, Sanskrit, Telugu, Hindi, Tamil, Bengali, Gujarati, Malayalam and Odia, all bundled in the app. Changing the language never translates or alters what you have written.</string>
    <string name="about_storage">Everything you enter is stored only on this device. The app needs no account and no internet connection, and it does not send your data anywhere.</string>
    <string name="about_pdf">Selected parts of a project can be exported as a PDF created on the device itself, with your profile in the header, tables, page numbers and a footer on every page.</string>
    <string name="about_fonts_title">Fonts and licences</string>
    <string name="about_fonts_note">The app bundles the Ubuntu font family (Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0) and Noto Sans fonts for the Indian scripts (SIL Open Font License 1.1). Their licence texts can be read below.</string>
    <string name="about_show_licences">Show licence texts</string>
    <string name="about_hide_licences">Hide licence texts</string>
    <string name="dvk_p1">Dr. Diddigi Vamsi Krishna is a Sanskrit scholar, manuscriptologist and researcher.</string>
    <string name="dvk_p2">He holds the M.A. and Ph.D. degrees.</string>
    <string name="dvk_p3">He is currently a Research Assistant at the Oriental Research Institute, University of Mysore, where he coordinates several major projects.</string>
    <string name="dvk_p4">He is the Founding Director of Shimshumara Shodha Pratishthanam, Mysuru.</string>
    <string name="dvk_p5">His research and scholarly contributions lie in Sanskrit studies and manuscriptology.</string>
    <string name="dvk_recognition_title">Recognition</string>
    <string name="dvk_recognition">Granthapuraskāra (ग्रन्थपुरस्कार), 2020, from Karnataka Samskrit University.</string>
    <string name="support_intro">Śodhamitra is free for everyone. If it helps your work, you may make a voluntary contribution towards its continued development.</string>
    <string name="support_optional">Contributions are entirely optional. Every research feature remains available without contributing.</string>
